  "rounds": {
    "1": {
      "note": "Sightseeing relies on a few useful patterns. <strong>hoi1 gei2 dim2</strong> (開幾點) = 'opens at what time' — works for shops, restaurants, anywhere with hours. <em>mun4 piu3</em> (門票) is your entry ticket; <em>jap6 coeng4</em> (入場) is the act of entering. Watch for <em>m4 ho2 ji5 paak3 ziu3</em> ('photos not allowed') signs at many HK museums and temples.",
      "words": [
        {
          "id": "attractions-001",
